dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in 4.4.1.stable and 4.0.stable. I didn't test any other versions\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.1.stable - Manjaro Linux #1 SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Thu Jul 17 22:09:32 UTC 2025 on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - AMD Radeon RX 6800 XT (radeonsi, navi21, LLVM 20.1.8, DRM 3.54, 6.6.99-1-MANJARO) - AMD Ryzen 5 2600X Six-Core Processor (12 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen using find and replace, it will overwrite any changes that have not yet been saved.\n\nIt appears as though the find and replace operates on the file on disk, then when the replace action is done, it will prompt you to reload any files that have been changed from disk, but this overwrites any unsaved changes because they don't appear in the file on disk.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Open any script in Godot's built in script editor.\n2. Type some text and do NOT save it.\n3. select some text (not the text from step 2) and press Ctrl-Shift-f to open the \"Find in Files\" dialogue\n4. press \"Replace...\" in the \"Find in Files\" dialogue\n5. (optional) type some replace text into the \"Replace:\" text box\n6. press \"Replace all (no undo)\" in the search results\n7. press \"Reload from disk\" in the \"Files have been modified outside Godot\" dialogue that pops up\n8. See that the replace text happened, but the text from step 2 is gone.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/u